      "hypothesis": "V35 raw fullfinancial forecast MSE improved but correction slightly worsened total MSE. Retest v18 bounded C/D expert mixing on the v35 daily fourclock financial forecasts, using actual paired-terminal feedback and date-joint calibration/meta resampling. This is a controlled method transfer, not a new algorithm discovery or a clock/month blacklist.",
      "source": "Reuse immutable independently verified v35 raw and as-issued calibrated forecasts, input/financial panels and fixed trade labels. Check all top-level, daily and training SHAs against committed v35 delivery manifest. Underlying base models remain daily-retrained on data available before that day; using cached issued forecasts does not freeze the economic model to one old month. No raw source downloads or uploads.",
      "meta_history": "Every day00ET, same whole-date terminal chronological prefix as v35. Stop at first feature-ready date with any unknown or not-yet-mature terminal; do not skip it. Among that prefix select latest120 dates with source full calibrated predictions actually ready for all3/4clocks. Min60 dates to enable correction learner. Both expert forecasts are their original as-issued values, not retrospectively refitted predictions. Current-day forecasts and labels excluded.",
      "warmup": "Source calibrated forecasts first ready2025-11-05; only39 issued days before Jan, found in pre-result coverage inspection. Until60mature meta dates, all adapted band routes preserve original source point/lower/199draws exactly (alpha1), rather than discard source forecasts. Unknown source remains cash. Adaptive point diagnostic omits band throughout. This fallback fixed before any new ledger outcomes.",
      "fit": "Transform two ETF expected net log returns to C=(L+S)/2,D=(L-S)/2. For each clock and component separately, minimize weighted sum[(raw+a(cal-raw)-truth)^2]+lambda(a-.5)^2 over0<=a<=1. Weights63datehalf-life totalN, divided across3/4clocks, then normalized for each head. Aggregate normalized rowweights by ORIGINAL DATE to compute neff=1/sum(dateweight^2). A=sumw(delta^2),B=sumw(delta*(truth-raw)),lambda=2A/neff; a=clip((B+lambda/2)/(A+lambda),0,1), or.5ifA<=1e-16. Same scalar loss as v18; no state-distance weights. Shared diagnostic pools all clocks but still date-based neff. For bootstrap, date multiplicities aggregate before neff.",
      "joint_bootstrap": "Use sorted union of current v35 calibration dates and meta dates.199circular10-date block draws,seed826+ETdateordinal. Same date multiplicity affects both fits, including overlapping dates even when pools start differently. Refit source partial-sharing calibration with own original dateweight normalization, weighted standardization and penalty20; refit clock/shared blend with perturbed meta weights and neff. Historical expert forecasts stay fixed as-issued. Current raw model held fixed; raw-training parameter uncertainty is not quantified.",
      "decision": "Current point=componentwise raw+alpha*(sourcecal-raw), restored toETF netlog scores. Each joint bootstrap predicts with its refit calibration and alpha. Joint radius=max(0,higher90% maxETF(draw-point)). Final radius=max(originalv35 radius,joint radius), so weakening calibration cannot automatically shrink safety margin below source. This empirical perturbation band is not a monthlyloss guarantee or a formally calibrated coverage interval. Greatestpositive point-radius (>1e-12) buys, tieSOXL; else cash. Same sourcefeature/pending-prefix gates. No targeted month or clock exemptions.",
